  "limitations": [
    "The sampling floor changes from 200 to 80 ms; the added initial-header component still caps at 200 ms. Other helper control logic is unchanged.",
    "All 36 timed files verify. Three rotating repetitions cover all order positions per cohort; D random faults are independent, not paired by seed.",
    "The shorter window improves C/D relative to the preserved adaptive baseline, but still loses D against v1.6.8 and Rust against zero helpers. B is mixed against the adaptive baseline. No general speed superiority or desktop adoption is accepted.",
    "C is a scaled 32 MiB exploration; B/D use standard sizes. Public E uses official publisher size/SHA-256 checks. F/G are not remeasured here.",
    "The standalone baseline-only command is a separate 8 MiB functional smoke and is not pooled into comparative timing medians. Its later parser correction changes argument validation/metadata only; each timing cohort retains its original harness snapshot/hash.",
    "Seven affected automatic-mode wire cases pass on each architecture; no new full 33-case claim.",
    "Known decoded lengths up to 1 TiB and strong ETag helpers remain diagnostic constraints. Desktop pause/cancel integration is absent.",
    "Published v1.6.8 remains 777ab94 with verified deployed packages and both actual updater paths. Its GUI/tray/cold-start limitation remains."
  ],
